    "created_at": "2024-08-02T10:44:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-02T10:44:41Z",
    "body": "Thank you for clarifying, @zcorpan - wow. that was really confusing.\r\nSo I guess we can close #10540 because its intent was not to change parsers, but to match parser behaviors.\r\n\r\nOnce entering PLAINTEXT, character tokens still emit, and even though `<` and `&` don't enter new states, IN BODY rules still apply to the character tokens.\r\n\r\nPerhaps I could update #10540 to clarify the wording and make this clearer.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
